  "context": [
    "This application supports students and residents in Toronto and the Greater Toronto and Hamilton Area, including people commuting to Toronto Metropolitan University (TMU, formerly Ryerson). This is a regional glossary, not evidence that a user attends TMU or made a particular trip. Only identify a merchant from its descriptor.",
    "PRESTO contactless debit descriptors can start PRES/ followed by a confirmation reference. PRESTO, TTC, GO Transit, UP Express, MiWay, Durham Region Transit (DRT), York Region Transit (YRT/Viva), Brampton Transit, Oakville Transit, Burlington Transit and Hamilton Street Railway (HSR) are transit systems: use TTC and PRESTO when the descriptor supports a fare or transit purchase. Do not infer the transit operator, station, route or a student fare from PRES/ alone. GO, UP, DRT, HSR, VIVA, PRES or METRO alone are ambiguous. PRESTO Pizza and TTC Treasury Services are not automatically transit fares.",
    "TMU/Ryerson can mean the university, not necessarily tuition. Explicit tuition or academic fees use Tuition and School; explicit textbooks, course supplies or printing use Textbooks and Supplies; food services or meal plans use Eating Out; residence payments use Housing. TMU Campus Store sells books, clothing and gifts: use Shopping unless the descriptor explicitly identifies books/supplies. TMU OneCard loads are multipurpose campus funds and TMU Financial Services handles different payments: identify the name but return null category without a specific purchase purpose. OneCard alone does not identify TMU.",
    "Metro store-number descriptors in Ontario are the grocery retailer, not a subway. Food Basics, FreshCo, Farm Boy, No Frills and Foody World are grocery brands. SDM with a store number and Canadian location means Shoppers Drug Mart. Shoppers Drug Mart, Dollarama, Canadian Tire, Gateway Newstands and convenience stores are mixed retailers: use Shopping, not an invented receipt item. Centex and Pioneer may sell fuel and convenience goods; their names alone do not identify the purchase.",
    "Bike Share Toronto is bicycle sharing, Green P is Toronto parking, and Toronto Hydro is the electricity utility (Housing). The current category list has no dedicated parking, fuel or bike-sharing category: identify clear names but return null category rather than calling them transit fares or rideshare. Bare abbreviations, location names, bank service-plan labels, payment processors and personal transfers do not identify a merchant.",
    "Canadian bank wrappers such as ONLINE PURCHASE, TELEPHONE ORDER and RECURRING PYMNT may precede a compact date and merchant. APPLE.COM/BILL may be apps, media or subscriptions; do not infer a recurring subscription from that label alone. Preserve trading names; do not expand FreshCo to a legal LLC or Canadian Tire to an invented company name."
  ],
